GtkAda4 basic application
========================

This project contains the code samples from the GtkAda User's Guide. It
includes a simple application that opens a window with a Quit button, and
an automated test of the samples for use in release sanity checks.

Copy this directory to a writable location before building. GNAT and
GPRbuild must be available in PATH. If GtkAda's installed project file is
not found automatically, add <prefix>/lib/gnat to GPR_PROJECT_PATH, where
<prefix> is the GtkAda installation prefix. When using shared libraries,
their directories must also be on the platform's library search path
(LD_LIBRARY_PATH on Linux, PATH on Windows).

To build and run the interactive application:

    gprbuild -p -P basic_application.gpr
    ./bin/ug_hello

Click Quit or close the window to exit. The main procedure is in
ug_hello.adb; the window and its callbacks are in ug_application.adb.
The basic_application.gpr project builds this application by default.

To build and run the automated sanity check against the installed library:

    gprbuild -p -P test.gpr
    ./bin/user_guide

The check exercises signal handlers, a custom button type, reference
counts, application activation and command-line handling. It opens and
closes windows automatically and returns zero when all checks pass.
Both programs require a graphical display. On a Linux machine without
a display, the sanity check can be run with Xvfb:

    GTK_A11Y=none GSETTINGS_BACKEND=memory GSK_RENDERER=cairo \
        xvfb-run -a ./bin/user_guide

On Windows, the executables have an .exe suffix.
